hello everyone in all my previous videos  I've been discussing things meant  directly for the students in this video  for a change I wish to discuss a few  things meant for the parents of the  students especially those students who  are preparing to leave for college for  the first time  the same time my hope is that some of  the points that I am going to discuss  will be relevant to the students of the  second year third year and Beyond so if  you're a student and you see that some  of the points are particularly relevant  for you I request you to please share it  with your parents discuss it with your  parents also and if you are a parent my  request is that please do not view this  video as me giving some sort of advice  to you I do not have the audacity to do  that you are the parents uh you as  parents have uh much more experience of  Parenthood compared to me so I will not  encroach on that responsibility on that  on that enormous responsibility but I  would still like to highlight a few  points based on the experiences that I  have had as a child myself through my  interactions with my own parents through  the interactions that I have seen that  my my friends have had with their  parents and finally through my  interactions with the parents of the  students for whom I was The Faculty  advisor over the last few years here in  the mechanical engineering department of  IIT kharagpur the main issue that I have  regarding the interaction that the  parents have with their students is that  either on the one hand their interaction  is too much like they try to exert too  much control or be too much involved uh  with their children  on the one hand and on the other hand  some of the parents they are not at all  involved so both of these extra extremes  is extremely harmful for the students  now let us consider the first case  where the parents exert too much control  or are too much involved with the  students day-to-day activities whether  it is curricular or co-curricular  activities  we have to understand one very important  thing that  college life is not just an opportunity  for the students to learn things  academically whether it is in the  lecture hall from the professors or from  the books or in the labs it is also an  extremely good opportunity for the  students to grow up to grow up as mature  independent human beings so if as  parents uh  you exert too much control over their  day-to-day activities you do not let  them  take responsibility for their own  decision making process I think it is a  complete loss of that tremendous  opportunity  now I'm not saying that you should  completely let the students fend for  themselves in their decision making  process be involved but  do not exert too much control  now I also understand that suddenly if  you remove all your  advice or your involvement it can be  tremendously harmful especially for  those students who have grown up in a  very protective fashion or perhaps they  have grown up in a very sheltered  fashion so if you do that abruptly if  you take away that control or that  involvement very abruptly it can be a  kind of shock to the students so that  also is not very good so my feeling is  that this should be done in a gradual  fashion let them take more and more  responsibility of the various kinds of  decisions because ultimately that is the  definition of being an adult taking  responsibility for your own decisions  now let us consider the Other Extreme  case where the parents are forget about  exerting control they are not even  involved and words sometimes they are  completely unaware of what is happening  in the student's career they are not  aware when the exams are taking place  they are not aware of what the results  of the students are  okay so this is extremely extremely  undesirable and unfortunate what happens  is that in these kinds of situations  slowly slowly the students realize that  their parents are not at all involved  and they end up  starting to lie to their parents  regarding their results I have actually  seen this happen so the parents are not  aware maybe sometimes or after one or  two or three semesters they randomly ask  their students or the children what are  their results and then just to avoid  some kind of an uncomfortable  conversation the students just lie to  their faces okay and the parents also  don't follow it up so this is extremely  extremely dangerous it is dangerous  because this kind of a situation can can  and actually have led to uh to a  scenario where the students start to  have backlog semester after semester and  then one unfortunate day the parents get  a phone call from The Institute or from  the Department from some Professor that  such and such a thing has happened to  the uh to the students progress it is  that that there is absolutely no  progress and the student has so many  backlogs and then the parents are at a  complete shock because remember that  most of these students have been very  very good students in their school life  and suddenly the parents hear through  this phone call that ah they are failing  in their subjects their children are  failing in the subjects they have  backlogs okay and I am not trying to  make it sound more dramatic than it  actually is I have personally have had  this feel this this experience of  calling up certain parents and informing  them of their students lack of progress  and it is an extremely heartbreaking  situation both for the parents as well  as for me as a professor okay so please  do not let the situation come to such a  pass that this kind of phone call has to  be made my request to all the parents is  that sure you will accompany more in  most cases you will accompany your  children at the time of admission and it  is a yearly event when we see that the  parents are accompanying their children  to the to the various markets within the  campus and they help to buy the the  blankets the brooms the buckets and and  that is absolutely fine so  my request is that please do not stop  your involvement after you have bought  these things to them okay your  responsibility your involvement does not  end with these blankets buckets and  brooms okay so uh please keep a periodic  track of what is actually happening in  their progress in their academic  progress and not just academic progress  it is absolutely inevitable that they  will develop some other kinds of  Interest also maybe in music in some  sports also keep a track of what they  are doing uh overall above all my  request to all parents is to please talk  to your children on a regular basis  it may not be on a daily basis but at  least over 2-3 days or maybe at least  once or twice a week you please make a  phone call to your students to your  children so now it is all almost all  students have their mobile phones uh  please make this call okay I know that  because they are all young adults they  may not like talking to you on this  regular basis they may resist taking  your advice I mean we have all done this  I mean you as parents of teenagers you  already know what I'm talking about uh  and probably when you were teenagers  yourself you also did like that so it is  uh this is the story of life children do  not listen to their parents uh but uh  my request to you is that despite their  resistance please talk to them if you  are a little bit patient and talk to  them manage to talk to them just a  little bit uh I think you already know  that even if they do not say it  explicitly to your face they do not  thank you but later on they will  definitely thank you okay we all know  this from our own experience  and  finally my request is that when the  students  try to tell you something please listen  Okay like  especially in middle class families what  happens is that the  Parents try to uh  look at their children especially when  when they go off to these kinds of  engineering and medical colleges to  completely  Outsource their own unfulfilled dreams  and aspirations on the shoulders of  their children  uh that is unfortunate okay so even if  they have already joined an engineering  on a Medical College uh  it is possible that some other kinds of  interests May develop in their mind in  their hearts please try to listen to  them and sometimes when you call them up  they may remain silent they may  ah  resist talking to you at all or they may  just  randomly say some things but in that  silence in that lack of words also there  may be a cry for help so I request all  of you to please try to listen to those  unsaid words from your students so these  are rather heavy words uh I do not want  to end this video on a rather solemn  note rather I want to end it on a very  very positive hopeful cheerful note so  I I sincerely pray and hope that after  you have left your children  in the campus or maybe if you are a  parent of a second year student third  year student and Beyond uh  the ultimate interactions that you are  going to have with your students when  they return to you after their campus  life will be a tremendously joyful one  where many of the dreams hopes and  aspirations not just from your side but  from their side also gets genuinely  fulfilled this is my hope and pray  prayers for everyone for each and every  family so thank you very much and all  the best to you your children and your  entire family thank you
 

